# Phase 3 skip-parse drill recon — rebuild after any grammar edit.
# Runtime requires the haxe-formatter fork checkout: set
# `ANYPARSE_HXFORMAT_FORK=/path/to/haxe-formatter` and run
# `node bin/recon.js` (or pass a single .hxtest path as argv[0] to
# probe one file).
#
# The output is repo-relative like every other hxml here, and that is
# load-bearing rather than tidy: it used to be the machine-global
# `/tmp/recon.js`, so two worker trees building this file wrote one
# artifact. Measured, 3 concurrent rounds from two worktrees: both
# builds exited 0 every round and the surviving `/tmp/recon.js` was
# one tree's twice and the other's once — the loser's `node` run then
# drilled a grammar it had not built, silently.
-cp src
-cp test
-lib hxnodejs
-main _ReconSkipParse
-js bin/recon.js
# Mirrors bin/apq-js.hxml — a corpus sweep is the work it measures. See there.
-D analyzer-optimize
